# Shell wait

Start a long repository command with `block_until_ms: 0`. Keep other work. The completion notice is the end signal.

Poll with AwaitShell only when the next step is blocked on that process. Wait for process exit, or for one line that means the whole command ended.

True end of complete `make verify`:

- `verified parent #100` after the last tracker check
- `make: *** [verify` when a make target fails

These lines are not the end of `make verify`:

- `verify-stage1` — contracts self-check, often near 15s
- a bare `Error:` — Storage Activation expected reject (`MissingOrInactive` / `IdentityMismatch`)

Size a poll window to the command class:

| Command | Typical duration |
|---|---|
| GitHub PR `verify` sentinel | about 16s |
| Dirty-tree `make verify` | fails in about 24s |
| One `verify-tracker` | tens of seconds |
| Clean complete `make verify` | about 9 minutes (Chrome exact-dist and isolated Recovery Copy) |

Use an 8–12 minute window only for one clean complete `make verify` when a poll is required, and only with a true end line.
